invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_mont_square returns without wiping its running sum,
  so the square before its last subtraction and the last row's multiple
  of the modulus stay in the dead frame after every square a signature
  makes. No output changes, so no vector notices.
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test copies the stack below a signature and finds
  two limbs of a value the signature held.

--- old
    ct_wipe(d, (k + 1) * sizeof(uint64_t));
    ct_wipe(t, (k + 2) * sizeof(uint64_t));
--- new
    ct_wipe(d, (k + 1) * sizeof(uint64_t));
